\section{Conclusion}\label{sec:conclusion}

NER exhibits oracle scaling ($c{\approx}0.5$) but aggregation fails above $\theta_{\text{crit}}{=}0.70$; entity construction and LP selection ($+0.3$\textendash$1.4$\,pp) bypass sample-level selection by operating at entity granularity.
The fundamental barrier is not that agreement signals lack information, but that this information does not translate into discriminative power at the sample level: $\alpha{\to}0$ even when $\rho$ is substantial.

